## Context
With the chooser gone, nobody has measured what LLM-chosen routing costs or
whether cross-family seats are actually selected. Quality deltas against the
old pins may be meaningless if the pins were inert (see 1063).

## Scope
Replay about 10 merged PRs with the `coaching` skill. Metrics: USD per PR and
the rate at which a cross-family seat is selected when one is reachable.
Estimated cost: a few USD and about 1 author-hour reading the diagnostics.
Drop the "vs old pins" comparison if 1063 shows the pins were inert. Judgment
seats (gaze, verify-gate) stay on standard-class recommendations until this
shows a cheaper model matches.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] USD per PR and cross-family rate reported, with the arithmetic shown
- [ ] `verify-adherence` still catches a known violation on an old PR under LLM-chosen routing
- [ ] Verdict recorded on whether review and gate seats may move to a cheaper model
